{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he looked.</b> Some interpret it as לבת אש (a flame of fire); the correct interpretation in my eyes is בלב האש (amidst the fire), for so we find: מה אמולה לבתך (Ezekiel 16). And R. Adninit said: if this were so, it would be בלבת with a chirik under the lamed, like אל גִנַת אגוז (Song of Songs 6:11) — and behold, he forgot וכְגַנָה זרועיה תצמיח (Isaiah 61:11)." "<b>The bush.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said that this is a species of thorn — 'and the good will of שוכני סנה' (Deuteronomy 33:16) is 'heaven,' and the meaning is 'upon the revered Name.' And R. Yeshuah said: the glory that dwelt in the bush — and he did not speak correctly, for how can he be called שוכני for a single moment? And further, why is it said in the pattern of an active participle? And it is not so: עשה שמים וארץ (Psalms 126:8) — for HaShem is continually making and sustaining them like the breath that proceeds from the mouth of man. And further, after he mentioned 'all מגד,' he mentioned lastly 'the will of HaShem.' And further, what reason is there to mention this angel? And further, it should have been 'the dweller in the bush,' with the definite article. In my opinion, every סנה is one and the same, and it is a species of dry thorn, and so it is in the language of Ishmael, and so Mount Sinai is named because of the סנה. And so interpret 'and the good will of שוכני סנה': the good will sought by the dweller in the place of the bush, that is, one who seeks and asks continually that HaShem do His will, and moistens his land in which he dwells — which was a dry place of bush — until the saturation comes and it becomes כגן רוה מלוחלח. And He informed him: מתוך הסנה (from the midst of the bush), with the definite article, for these are the words of Moses as he wrote the Torah. And בוער is from the binyan of active verbs, for אש בוערה is like אש אוכלה (Deuteronomy 4:24), and the proof is כאש תבער יער (Psalms 83:15). And behold, the fire that was in the bush burned all that surrounded it, for this is like שלחו באש מקדשך (Psalms 74:7), and so ההר בוער באש (Deuteronomy 5:20)." "And the word אֻכָּל is an adjective like פעול, and like it אם תראה אותי לוקח מאתך (2 Kings 2:10), which has a kamatz, and so לנער היולד (Judges 13:8), כהם יוקשים בני האדם (Ecclesiastes 9:12). And these are active participles; therefore ורגל מוּעָדֶת (Proverbs 25:19) is not like them, for it has a shureq under the cholam, and it is like פועלת."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved 'R. Adninit' as printed; identity uncertain but treated as a proper name."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:20.897437048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}